{
  "case_id": "2008-08-6",
  "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Kenneth M. Rosenstein",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State of Alaska fully recognizes the importance of DNA evidence. The State provides criminal defendants with pretrial access to that evidence and it has postconviction procedures that give prisoners a fair opportunity to retest that evidence should new technology become available."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, he's -- he's not at this point. All he's doing is seeking evidence. We don't know -- he doesn't know presumably -- exactly what that evidence is going to show. The evidence may prove to be exonerating and it may not be."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there any reason to think that if, in fact -- sorry."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Neal K. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit created a novel constitutional right by extending Brady to the postconviction setting. Mr. Osborne doesn't attempt to defend that rationale. Instead, he attempts to mint a"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What were the two confessions? I know the one before the parole authorities. What was the other one?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position, Justice Scalia, is that there is no constitutional right to DNA, but if -- were the Court inclined to find one and locate it somewhere in Brady or the procedural due process clause, something we think which would be very difficult to do, but were it -- if that were the Court's inclination, absolutely, it should at least mirror the Federal statute and the -- and the rock solid requirements of 3600, which do require that perjury -- that perjury statement to be made in order to --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I agree with that, Your Honor. I mean, not only is Alaska not making a claim that he did not act with due diligence here, but they're not doing -- they're making that claim for a reason."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress is a marvelous statute that no one is -- is questioning one bit. It is odd that the Solicitor General walks into this courtroom and asks this Court to adopt a materiality test that was rejected by Congress."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Neufeld",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is, is that the test that they're calling for here is irrational; that it's completely irrational when you have something as powerful and new as DNA evidence, which can conclusively -- unlike any other forensic discipline that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "you will see cases where 50 percent of the judges that reviewed those cases found the evidence to be very compelling evidence of guilt or indeed overwhelming evidence of guilt, but nonetheless DNA trumped all that evidence and excluded those."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you have a constitutional right to the DNA evidence if the accuracy of the test was the same as the one that your counsel submitted at trial?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. NEUFELD",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. NEUFELD: Under the Constitution there is no duty under current law to preserve the evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: May I -- may I just ask one point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. ROSENSTEIN",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROSENSTEIN: Justice Ginsburg, Mr. Osborne by filing an affidavit that would accompany his application, that would -- I think that would operate to state a claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-6",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "a69bd8d00b97df8a5d27af015943b69cc2173db2f01af04ee9653b371b764b64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a69bd8d00b97-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
